hadiths[303]{hadithnumber,text}:
"149","Jabir bin Abdullah narrated that :Allah's Messenger said: \Jibril led me (in Salat)\"". He mentioned something similar to the Hadith of Ibn Abbas (no. 149) in meaning"""""
"150","Abu Hurairah narrated that :Allah's Messenger said: \Indeed for (the time of) Salat (there is a) beginning and an end. The beginning of the time for the Zuhr prayer is when the sun passes the zenith"""""
"151","Sulaiman bin Buraidah narrated that his father said:\A man came to the Prophet to ask him about the times for Salat. So he said: 'Stay with us"""""
"152","Aishah narrated:\Allah's Messenger would pray Subh (at such time that) the women would leave (after the prayer)\"" - AI-AnsarI (one of the narrators) said - the women would pass by wrapped in their Mirts and they would not be recognizable due to the darkness.\"" And Qutaibah said: \""covered.\"" (instead of \""wrapped)"""""
"153","Rafi bin Khadlj said:\I heard Allah's Messenger saying: 'Perform Fajr at AI-Isfar"""""
"154","Aishah narrated:\I have not seen anyone who hastened Zuhr more than Allah's Messenger nor Abu Bakr"""""
"155","Anas bin Malik narrated:\Allah's Messenger prayed Zuhr when the sun had passed the zenith"""""
"156","Abu Hurairah narrated that :Allah's Messenger said: \In very hot weather"""""
"157","Abu Dharr narrated:\Allah's Messenger was on a journey and Bilal was with him. So he wanted to call for the prayer"""""
"158","Urwah narrated from Aishah:\Allah's Messenger prayed Asr while the sun was (shining) in her chamber"""""
"159","Al-Ala bin Abdur-Raman narrated that :he visited Anas bin Malik in his home in Al Basrah after finishing Zuhr"
"160","Umm Salamah narrated:\Allah's Messenger would hasten Zuhr more than you (people)"""""
"161","Narrator not mentioned:[And I have in my book: \Ali bin Hujr informed me from lsma'il bin Ibrahim"""""
"162","Similar narration is reported by Bishr ibn Mu'adh Al-Bari who said that :Isma'il ibn Ulayyah narrated to him from Ibn Juraij. This latter chain is more correct"
"163","Salmah bin AI-Akwa narrated:\Allah's Messenger prayed Maghrib when the sun had set and it (the sun) had hidden in the veil (of darkness)"""""
"164","An-Nu'man bin Bashir said:\I am the most knowledgeable among the people about the prescribed time of this prayer: Allah's Messenger would pray it when the moon set on the third (of the month)"""""
"165","An-Nu'man bin Bashir said:A similar narration (from another chain linking to) this chain is also reported"
"166","Abu Hurairah narrated that :Allah's Messenger said: \If it were not that it would be a hardship on my Ummah"""""
"167","Abu Barzah narrated:\The Prophet would dislike to sleep before Isha and to talk after it"""""
"168","Umar bin Al-Khattab narrated:\Allah's Messenger would talk during the night with Abu Bakr about matters concerning the Muslims while I was with them"""""
"169","Umm Farwah - and she was one of those who gave pledge of allegiance to the Prophet - narrated:\The Prophet was asked: 'Which deed is the best?' So he said: 'Salat in the beginning of its time"""""
"170","Ali bin AbI Talib narrated that :the Prophet said to him: 'Ali! Three are not to be delayed: Salat when its time comes"
"171","Ibn Umar narrated that :Allah's Messenger said: \The beginning of the time for Salat is pleasing to Allah"""""
"172","Abu Amr Ash-Shaibani narrated:\A man said to Ibn Mas'ud: 'Which deed is most virtuous?' He said: 'I asked Allah's Messenger (that). He said: \""Salat at the beginning of its time.\"" I asked him: \""What is after that O Messenger of Allah?\"" He said: \""Being dutiful to one's parents.\"" I said: \""What is after that [O Messenger of Allah]?\"" He said: \""Jihad in the Way of Allah"""""
"173","Aishah narrated:\Allah's Messenger did not pray any Salat at the end of its time two times"""""
"174","Aishah narrated:""Allah's Messenger did not pray any Salat at the end of its time two times, until Allah took him"
"175","Abu Dharr narrated that :the Prophet said: \O Abu Dharr! There will be leaders after me who cause the Salat to die; so perform the Salat during its time. If you pray (with them) during its time"""""
"176","Abu Qatadah narrated:\They asked the Prophet about when they sIept past the Salat. He said: 'There is no negligence in sleep"""""
"177","Anas (bin Malik) narrated that :Allah's Messenger said: \Whoever forgets a Salat then he is to pray it when he remembers it"""""
"178","Abdullah (bin Mas'ud] narrated:\The idolaters kept Allah's Messenger distracted from four prayers on the Day of Al-Khandaq (the battle of the Trench) until as much as Allah willed of the night had passed. So he ordered Bilal to call the Adhan"""""
"179","Jabir bin Abdullah narrated:\On the Day of Al-Khandaq (the battle of the Trench)"""""
"180","Abdullah bin Mas'ud narrated that :Allah's Messenger said: \Salatul-Wusta is the Asr prayer"""""
"181","Smurah bin Jundub narrated that :the Prophet said: \Salatul-wusta is the Asr prayer"""""
"182","Ibn Abbas narrated:\I head more than one of the Companions of the Prophet; Umar bin Al-Khattab among"""""
"183","Ibn Abbas narrated:\The Prophet only performed the two rak'ah (units of prayer) after Asr because some wealth came to him which distracted him from the two rak'ah after Zuhr"""""
"184","Abdullah bin Mughaffal narrated that :the Prophet said: \Between every two calls (to prayer) there is a Salat for whoever wills"""""
"185","Abu Hurairah narrated that :the Prophet said: \Whoever catches a Rak'ah of Subh before the sun has risen"""""
"186","Abu Hurairah narrated that :the Prophet said: ""Whoever catches a Rak'ah of Subh before the sun has risen, then he has caught Subh. Whoever catches a Rak'ah of Asr before the sun has set, then he has caught Asr"
"187","Ibn Abbas narrated that :the Prophet said: \Whoever combines two prayers without any excuse then he has committed something from the major sins"""""
"188","Narrated Abu Salamah, Yahya ibn Khalaf al-Basri: al-Mu'tamir ibn Sulayman narrated to us, from his father, from Hanash, from 'Ikrimah, from Ibn 'Abbas ṣallallahu 'alayhi wa sallam, from the Prophet ﷺ, who said:\n\n**\Whoever combines two prayers without having an excuse has approached one of the gates of major sins.\""**\n\nAbu 'Isa [al-Tirmidhi] commented: This Hanash is Abu 'Ali al-Rahabi"
"189","**Sa'id ibn Yahya ibn Sa'id al-Umawi narrated to us:** My father narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Ishaq narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ibrahim ibn al-Harith al-Taymi, from Muhammad ibn 'Abdullah ibn Zayd, from his father, who said:\n\n\When we awoke in the morning"
"190","Abu Mahdhurah narrated that :Allah's Messenger sat with him and taught him the Adhan word for word. Ibrahim said"
"191","Abu Mahdhurah narrated that :the Prophet taught him the Adhan with nineteen phrases"
"192","Anas bin Malik narrated:\Bilal was ordered to make the phrases of the Adhan even"""""
"193","Abdullah bin Zaid said:\Allah's Messenger would say each phrase of the call (for prayer) two times"""""
"194","Jabir [bin Abdullah] narrated:\Allah's Messenger said to Bilal: \""O Bilal! When you call the Adhan then do so deliberately and slowly"""""
"195","Jabir [bin Abdullah] narrated:(Another chain for) a similar narration (as no)"
"196","Abd ibn Humayd narrated to us: Yunus ibn Muhammad narrated to us, from Abd al-Munim, a similar narration. Abu Isa (al-Tirmidhi) said: This hadith of Jabir is a hadith that we do not know except through this chain of narration, from the hadith of Abd al-Munim, and it is an unknown chain of narration (isnad majhul), and Abd al-Munim is a sheikh from Basra."
"197","Bilal narrated:\Allah's Messenger said [to me]: 'Do not say the Tathwib for any prayer except the Fajr prayer.'\"" [He said:] There is something on this topic from Abu Mahdhurah. Abu `Eisa said: We do not know of the Hadith of Bilal except as a narration of Abu Isra'il Al-Mula'i. Abu Isra'il did not hear this Hadith from Al-Hakam bin `Utaibah. He said: He only reported it from Al-Hasan bin `Umarah"""""
"198","Ziyad bin Al-Harith As-Suda'i narrated:\Allah's Messenger ordered me to call the Adhan for the Fajr prayer. I called the Adhan"""""
"199","Abu Hurairah narrated that :Allah's Messenger said: \None should call the Adhan except for one with Wudu"""""
"200","Ibn Shihab narrated that :Abu Hurairah said: \None should call (for the prayer except for one with Wudu)"""""
"201","Jabir bin Samurah narrated:The Mu'adh-dhin of Allah's Messenger would wait and he would not call the Iqamah until he saw the Allah's Messenger had come out"
"202","Salim narrated from his father (Ibn Umar) that :the Prophet said: \Indeed Bilal calls the Adhan in the night"""""
"203","Abu Ash-Sha'tha said:\A man exited the Masjid after the Adhan for Asr had been called. So Abu Hurairah said: 'As for this person"""""
"204","Malik bin Al-Huwairih said:\A cousin of mine and I arrived as guests of Allah's Messenger. He said to us: 'When you travel then call the Adhan and Iqamah and let the eldest of you lead the prayer"""""
"205","Ibn Abbas narrated:\The Prophet said: 'Whoever calls the Adhan for seven years"""""
"206","Abu Hurairah narrated that :Allah's Messenger said: \The Imam is answerable and the Mu'adh-dhin is entrusted. O Allah! Guide the Imams and pardon the Mu'adh-dhins"""""
"207","Abu Sa'eed narrated that :Allah's Messenger said: \Whenyou hear the call (to prayer) then say the similar to what the Mu'adh-dhin says"""""
"208","**Narrated by Abu Sa'id (may Allah be pleased with him):**\n\nHe said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said:\n\n**\When you hear the call to prayer (Adhan)"
"209","Sa'd bin Abi Waqqas narrated that :Allah's Messenger said: \Whoever says"""""
"210","Jabir bin Abdullah narrated that :Allah's Messenger said: \Whoever says"""""
"211","Anas bin Malik narrated that :Allah's Messenger said: \The supplication made between the Adhan and Iqamah is not rejected"""""
"212","Narrated by Anas ibn Malik (may Allah be pleased with him), who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said:\n\n**\Du'a (supplication) is not rejected between the Adhan and the Iqamah.\""**\n\nAbu Isa (al-Tirmidhi) said: The hadith of Anas is a hadith that is hasan (good). It was also narrated by Abu Ishaq al-Hamdani from Burayd ibn Abi Maryam from Anas from the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) with a similar narration."""""
"213","Abu Hurairah narrated that :Allah's Messenger said: \The five prayers"""""
"214","Ibn Umar narrated that :Allah's Messenger said: \Salat in congregation is twenty-seven degrees more virtuous than a man's Salat alone"""""
"215","Abu Hurairah narrated that :Allah's Messenger said: \Indeed a man's Salat in the congregation is increased by twenty five rewards over his Salat alone"""""
"216","Abu Hurairah narrated that :the Prophet said: \I was about to order my boys to collect bundles of firewood"""""
"217","Mujahid said:\Ibn Abbas was asked about a man who fasted during the day and stood (in prayers) during the night"""""
"218","Jabir hin Yazid hin Al-Aswad [Al-Amir] narrated that his father said:\I attended Hajj with the Prophet. I prayed the Subh (Fajr) prayer with him in Masjid AI-Khaif.\"" He said: \""When the Prophet finished"""""
"219","Jabir hin Yazid hin Al-Aswad [Al-Amir] narrated that his father said:""I attended Hajj with the Prophet. I prayed the Subh (Fajr) prayer with him in Masjid AI-Khaif."" He said: ""When the Prophet finished, he turned (from the Qiblah) and saw two men at the back of the people who had not prayed with him. He said, 'Bring them to me.' So I brought then while they were shuddering with fear. He said: 'What prevented you from praying with us?"" They said: 'O Messenger of Allah!' We prayed at our camp.' So he said: 'Do not do that; when you pray in your camp then you come to a Masjid with a congregation, then pray with them. That will be a voluntary prayer for you"
"220","Uthman bin Affan narrated that :Allah's Messenger said: \Whoever attends Isha (prayer) in congregation"""""
"221","Jundub bin Sufyan narrated that :the Prophet said: \Whoever prays the Subh then he is under the protection of Allah's covenant"""""
"222","Buraidah Al-Aslami narrated that :the Prophet said: \Give glad tiding to those who walk to the Masajid in the dark; of a complete light on the Day of Resurrection"""""
"223","Abu Hurairah narrated that :Allah's Messenger said: \The best rows for the men are the first of them"""""
"224","Narrator not mentioned:And the Prophet said: \If the people knew what (reward) is in the call (Adhan) and the first row"""""
"225","The Prophet (peace be upon him) said: \If the people knew what is in the call to prayer (Adhan) and the first row (of prayer)"
"226","An-Nu'man bin Bashir said:\Allah's Messenger would straighten our lines. One day he came out and saw a man whose chest was protruding from the people"""""
"227","Abdullah (Ibn Masud) narrated that :the Prophet said: \Let those among you with understanding and reason be close to me"""""
"228","Abdullah (Ibn Masud) narrated that :the Prophet said: ""Let those among you with understanding and reason be close to me, then those after them, then those after them. And do not separate or dissention will occur among your hearts, and beware of the commotion of the markets"
"229","Hilal bin Yasar said:\Ziyad bin Abi Al-Ja'd took me by the hand while we were in Ar Raqqah"""""
"230","Wabisah bin Ma'bad narrated:\A man prayed alone behind the row s the Prophet ordered him to repeat the Salat"""""
"231","Ibn Abbas narrated:\I prayed with the Prophet one night. I stood at his left"""""
"232","Samurah bin Jundub narrated:\Allah's Messenger ordered us that when we were three"""""
"233","Anas bin Malik narrated:\My grandmother Mutalikah invited Allah's Messenger to a meal that she prepared. He ate from it"""""
"234","Abu Mas'ud narrated that :Allah's Messenger said: \The one who recites most of the Book of Allah is to lead the people (in prayers). If they are equal in recitation"""""
"235","Abu Hurairah narrated that :the Prophet said: \When one of you leads the people in prayer then let him be brief"""""
"236","Anas [bin Malik] narrated:\Allah's Messenger was among the lightest of people in Salat with its completeness"""""
"237","Abu Sa'eed narrated that :Allah's Messenger said: \the key to Salat is the purification"""""
"238","Abu Hurairah narrated:\When Allah's Messenger performed the Takbir for Salat he would spread his fingers"""""
"239","Abu Hurairah narrated:\When Allah's Messenger would enter the Salat he would raise his hands while they were extended"""""
"240","Anas bin Malik narrated that :Allah's Messenger said: \Whoever performs Salat for Allah for forty days in congregation"""""
"241","Abu Sa'eeed Al Khudri narrated:\When Allah;s Messenger stood for Salat during the night"""""
"242","Aishah narrated:\When the Prophet opened the Salat he would say: (Subhanaka Allahumma wa bihamdika wa tabarakasmuka"""""
"243","Narrated by al-Hasan ibn 'Arafah and Yahya ibn Musa, who both said: Abu Mu'awiyah narrated to us, from Harithah ibn Abi al-Rijal, from 'Amrah, from 'Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her), who said:\n\n\When the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) began the prayer"
"244","Ibn Abbas narrated:\The Prophet would open his Salat with (Bismillahir-Rahmanir-Rahim)"""""
"245","**Narrated by Ibn ‘Abbās (raḍiya Allāhu ‘anhumā):**\n\n\The Prophet (ṣallallāhu ‘alayhi wa sallam) used to commence his prayer with *Bismillāhir-Raḥmānir-Raḥīm* (In the Name of Allah"
"246","Ubadah bin As-Samil narrated that :the Prophet said: \There is no Salat for the one who does not recite Fatihatil-Kitab"""""
"247","Wa'il bin Hujr narrated:\I heard the Prophet recite: (Not (the way) of those who earned Your anger"""""
"248","Bundar Muhammad ibn Bashshar narrated to us: Yahya ibn Sa'id and Abd al-Rahman ibn Mahdi narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us from Salamah ibn Kuhayl, from Hujr ibn Anbas, from Wa'il ibn Hujr, who said: I heard the Prophet ﷺ recite: ""Not of those who have evoked [Your] anger or of those who are astray"" (1:7), then he said: ""Amin,"" and he prolonged his voice with it. He said: In this chapter there are narrations from Ali and Abu Hurayrah. Abu Isa said: The hadith of Wa'il ibn Hujr is hasan. More than one of the people of knowledge among the Companions of the Prophet ﷺ, the Tabi'in, and those after them act upon this, holding that the man raises his voice with the amin and does not conceal it. Al-Shafi'i, Ahmad, and Ishaq hold this view. Shu'bah narrated this hadith from Salamah ibn Kuhayl from Hujr Abu al-Anbas from Alqamah ibn Wa'il from his father that the Prophet ﷺ recited: ""Not of those who have evoked [Your] anger or of those who are astray,"" then he said ""Amin,"" and he lowered his voice with it. Abu Isa said: I heard Muhammad say: The hadith of Sufyan in this is more authentic than the hadith of Shu'bah, and Shu'bah erred in several places in this hadith: he said ""from Hujr Abu al-Anbas,"" but he is Hujr ibn Anbas, and his kunya is Abu al-Sakin. He added ""from Alqamah ibn Wa'il,"" but there is no Alqamah in it; rather it is from Hujr ibn Anbas from Wa'il ibn Hujr. And he said ""he lowered his voice with it,"" but it is ""he prolonged his voice with it."" Abu Isa said: I asked Abu Zur'ah about this hadith, and he said: The hadith of Sufyan in this is more authentic than the hadith of Shu'bah. He said: Al-Ala ibn Salih al-Asadi narrated from Salamah ibn Kuhayl similar to the narration of Sufyan."
"249","Abu Hurairah narrated that :the Prophet said \When the Imam says 'Amin' then (all of you) say 'Amin.' For whoever's 'Amin' concurs with the 'Amin' of the angels"""""
"250","Al-Hasan narrated that :Samurah said: \there are two pauses that I preserved from Allah's Messenger.\"" But Imran bin Husain rejected that and said: \""We preserved one pause.\"" \""So we wrote to Ubayy bin Ka'b in Al-Madinah. Ubayy wrote that Samurah was correct.\"" Sa'eed said: \""We said to Qatadah: 'What are those two pauses?' He said: 'When he entered into his Salat"""""
"251","Qabisah bin Hulb narrated from :his father who said: \Allah's Messenger lead us in prayer and hold his left hand with his right"""""
"252","Abdullah bin Mas'ud narrated:\Allah's Messenger would say the Takbir for every lowering and raising"""""
"253","Abu Hurairah narrated:\Allah's Messenger would say the Takhir while he was going down"""""
"254","Salim narrated from :his father (Ibn Umar) who said: \I saw Allah's Messenger when he opened the Salat"""""
"255","Narrated by Qutaybah and Ibn Abi 'Umar, who both narrated from Sufyan ibn 'Uyaynah, from al-Zuhri, from Salim, from his father, who said:\n\n\I observed the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) raising his hands when commencing the prayer until they were level with his shoulders"
"256","Alqamah narrated that :Abdullah bin Mas'ud said: \Shall I not demonstrate the Salat of Allah's Messenger to you?\"" Then he offered Salat and he did not raise his hands except while saying the first Takbir"""""
"257","Abu Abdur-Rahman As-Sulami said:\Umar bin Al-Khattab [may Allah be pleased with him] said to us: 'The knees are the Sunnah for you"""""
"258","**Narrated by Ahmad ibn Mani': Abu Bakr ibn Ayyash narrated to us, from Abu Husayn, from Abu 'Abd ar-Rahman as-Sulami, who said:**\n\n'Umar ibn al-Khatṭāb, may Allah be pleased with him, said to us: \Indeed"
"259","Sa'd bin Abi Waqas said:""We would do that, but then we were prohibited from it, and we were ordered to put our hands on our knees"
"260","Ibn Mas'ud narrated that :the Prophet said: \When one of you bows then says while he is bowing: (Subhana Rabbiyal Azim) 'Glorious is my Lord the Magnificent' three times"""""
"261","Ibn Mas'ud narrated that :the Prophet said: \When one of you bows then says while he is bowing: (Subhana Rabbiyal Azim) 'Glorious is my Lord the Magnificent' three times"
"262","(Another similar narration) This Hadith has been narrated from Hudhaifah :from another route: \That he performed Salat during the night with the Prophet\"" and he mentioned the Hadith"""""
"263","Ali bin Abi Talib narrated:\The Prophet prohibited wearing Qassi"""""
"264","Abu Mas'ud Al-Ansari [Al-Badri] narrated that :Allah's Messenger said: \The Salat is not acceptable if a man is not at rest - meaning his back - while bowing and prostrating"""""
"265","Ali bin Abi Talib narrated:\When Allah's Messenger would raise his head from bowing he would say: (Sami Allahi liman hamidal. Rabba na lakal-hamd"""""
"266","Abu Hurairah narrated that :Allah's Messenger said: \When the Imam says: (Sami Allahu liman hamidah) 'Allah listens to those who praise Him. Then (all of you) say: (Rabbana wa lakal-hamd) 'O our Lord! And to You is the praise for whoever's saying concurs with the saying of the angels"""""
"267","Wa'il bin Hujr narrated:\I saw Allah's Messenger when he prostrated placing his knees (on the ground) before his hands"""""
"268","Abu Hurairah narrated that :the Prophet said; \Is it that one of you intends to kneel in his Salat with the kneeling of the camel?"""""
"269","Abu Hurairah narrated that :the Prophet said; ""Is it that one of you intends to kneel in his Salat with the kneeling of the camel?"
"270","Abu Ishaq narrated:\I said to Al-Bara bin Azib: 'Where would the Prophet place his face when he prostrated?' He said: 'Between his hands"""""
"271","Al-Abbas bin Abdul-Muttalib narrated that he heard :Allah's Messenger Saying: \When the worshipper prostrates with him: His face"""""
"272","Ibn Abbas narrated:\The Prophet ordered that one prostrate on seven bones and that he not gather his hair nor his garment"""""
"273","Ubaidallah bin Abdullah bin Arqam Al-Khuza'I narrated from his father (Abdullah bin Arqam)"
"274","Abu Kurayb narrated to us: Abu Khalid al-Ahmar narrated to us from Dawud ibn Qays, from Ubayd Allah ibn Abd Allah ibn al-Aqram al-Khuza'i, from his father, who said: I was with my father at al-Qa' of Namirah when a mounted group passed by, and there was the Messenger of Allah ﷺ standing in prayer. He said: I used to look at the whiteness of his armpits when he prostrated. He said: In this chapter there are narrations from Ibn Abbas, Ibn Buhaynah, Jabir, Ahmar ibn Juz, Maymunah, Abu Humayd, Abu Mas'ud, Abu Usayd, Sahl ibn Sa'd, Muhammad ibn Maslamah, al-Bara ibn Azib, Adi ibn Amir, and Aishah. Abu Isa said: This Ahmar ibn Juz is a man from the Companions of the Prophet ﷺ who has a single hadith. Abu Isa said: The hadith of Abd Allah ibn al-Aqram is hasan; we do not know it except from the hadith of Dawud ibn Qays, and we do not know of any other hadith from Abd Allah ibn al-Aqram al-Khuza'i from the Prophet ﷺ except this one. The practice is upon this according to the majority of the people of knowledge among the Companions of the Prophet ﷺ. He said: Abd Allah ibn al-Aqram al-Khuza'i has only this hadith from the Prophet ﷺ. Abd Allah ibn Arqam al-Zuhri is a Companion of the Prophet ﷺ, and he was the scribe of Abu Bakr al-Siddiq."
"275","Anas narrated that :Allah's Messenger said: \Be balanced in the prostration"""""
"276","Amir bin Sa'd [bin Abi Waqqas] narrated from his father:\The Prophet ordered placing the hands (on the ground) keeping the feet erect. (by resting feet on the toes and making the tips of the toes facing the Qiblah)"""""
"277","(Another chain that) Amir bin Sa'd narrated:\The Prophet ordered placing the hands (on the ground).\"" And he mentioned in it: \""From his father"""""
"278","Al-Bara bin Azib narrated:\The Salat of Allah's Messenger (was such that) when he bowed"""""
"279","Narrated to us Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Musa al-Marwazi, that Abdullah ibn al-Mubarak informed them, that Shu'bah informed them, from al-Hakam, from Abdur-Rahman ibn Abi Laila, from al-Bara' ibn Azib, who said:\n\n\The prayer of the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) — when he performed ruku' (bowing)"
"280","Al-Bara said:\When we performed Salat behind Allah's Messenger"""""
"281","Ali narrated:\Allah's Messenger said to me: 'O Ali! I love for you what I love for myself"""""
"282","Tawus said:\We asked Ibn Abbas about squatting (sitting) on the heels. He said: 'It is the Sunnah.' We said: 'We think that it is difficult for a man.' He said: 'Rather"""""
"283","**Narrated by Abu Dawud and al-Tirmidhi:**\n\nYahya ibn Musa narrated to us, Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Ibn Jurayj informed us, Abu al-Zubayr informed me that he heard Tawus say:\n\n\We said to Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with him) regarding *al-iq'a'* (sitting with the buttocks placed upon the heels) between the two prostrations. He said: 'It is the Sunnah.' We said: 'Indeed"
"284","Narrated by Salamah ibn Shabib, from Zayd ibn Hubab, from Kamil Abu al-'Ala', from Habib ibn Abi Thabit, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn 'Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both), that the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) used to say between the two prostrations:\n\n\O Allah"
"285","Abu Hurairah narrated:\[Some of] the Companions of the Prophet complained [to the Prophet] about the hardship of the prostration on them"""""
"286","Malik bin Al-Huwairith Al-Laithi narrated that he saw :Allah's Messenger performing Salat. When he was in an odd number of his Salat"
"287","Abu Hurairah narrated:\Allah's Messenger would get up during his Salat on the tips of his feet"""""
"288","**Narrated by Abu Hurayrah (may Allah be pleased with him):**\n\nHe said: \The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) would rise during prayer upon the tops of his feet (i.e."
"289","Ibn Abbas narrated:\Allah's Messenger would teach us the Tashah-hud just as he would teach us the Qur'an. He would say: (At-Tahiyyatu"""""
"290","Ibn Abbas narrated:""Allah's Messenger would teach us the Tashah-hud just as he would teach us the Qur'an. He would say: (At-Tahiyyatu, al mubarakatu, as-salawatu at-tayyibatulillah. Salamun alaika ayyuhan-naibiyyu wa rahmatullahi wa barakatuhu, salamun alaina wa ala ibadalillahis-salihin. Ashhadu an la ilaha illallah, wa ashhadu anna Muhammadan abduhu wa Raduluh.) 'All greetings, goodness, prayers, and pure words are for Allah. Peace be upon you O Prophet, and Allah's mercy and His blessings, Peace be upon us and all of the righteous worshippers of Allah. I testify that there is none worthy of worship except Allah, and I testify that Muhammad is Allah's worshipper and Messenger"
"291","Abū Saʿīd al-Ashajj narrated to us: Yūnus ibn Bukayr narrated to us, from Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq, from ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn al-Aswad, from his father, from ʿAbdullāh ibn Masʿūd (may Allāh be pleased with him), who said: \It is from the Sunnah to recite the Tashahhud quietly.\""\n\nAbū ʿĪsā (al-Tirmidhī) said: \""The Ḥadīth of Ibn Masʿūd is a ḥasan gharīb ḥadīth"
"292","Abū Kurayb narrated to us: ʿAbdullāh ibn Idrīs narrated to us: ʿĀṣim ibn Kulayb al-Jarmī narrated from his father, from Wāʾil ibn Ḥujr, who said: \I came to Madīnah"
"293","Abbas bin SAhl [bin Sa'd] narrated:""Abu Humaid, Abu Usaid, Sahl bin Sa'd, and Muhammad bin Maslamah were once together and they were mentioning the Salat of Allah's Messenger. Abu Humaid said: ""I am the most knowledgeable among you of the Salat of Allah's Messenger: Indeed Allah's Messenger sat - meaning for Tashah-hud - he spread his left foot, and made the top of his right (foot) face the Qiblah, and he placed his right hand on his right knee, and his left hand on his left knee, and indicated with his finger - meaning the index finge"
"294","Abdullah narrated:\The Prophet would say the Salam from his right and from his left (saying): (As-Salamu alaikum wa rahmatullah"""""
"295","Aishah narrated:\Allah's Messenger would say one Taslim for the Salat while facing forward and turning to his right side a little"""""
"296","**Muḥammad ibn Yaḥyā al-Naysābūrī narrated to us, ʿAmr ibn Abī Salamah Abū Ḥafṣ al-Tinnīsī narrated to us, from Zuhayr ibn Muḥammad, from Hishām ibn ʿUrwah, from his father, from ʿĀʾishah (may Allāh be pleased with her), that the Messenger of Allāh (peace and blessings be upon him) used to perform the *taslīm* (salutation of conclusion) in the prayer with a single *taslīm* facing his face, inclining slightly toward the right side.**\n\n**He (Abū ʿĪsā) said:** And there are narrations on this topic from Sahl ibn Saʿd (may Allāh be pleased with him).\n\n**Abū ʿĪsā (al-Tirmidhī) said:** The ḥadīth of ʿĀʾishah (may Allāh be pleased with her) is not known to us as *marfūʿ* (elevated to the Prophet ﷺ) except through this chain of narration.\n\n**Muḥammad ibn Ismāʿīl (al-Bukhārī) said:** Zuhayr ibn Muḥammad — the people of Shām (Greater Syria) narrate *munkar* (objectionable) reports from him, whereas the narrations of the people of ʿIrāq from him are more sound and more reliable.\n\n**Muḥammad (al-Bukhārī) said:** Aḥmad ibn Ḥanbal said: \It is as though the Zuhayr ibn Muḥammad who came to them is not the same one from whom narrations are transmitted in ʿIrāq; it is as though he were another man whose name was confused (or altered).\""\n\n**Abū ʿĪsā (al-Tirmidhī) said:** Some of the scholars have held this view regarding the *taslīm* in the prayer. However"
"297","Aishah narrated:\When Allah's Messenger said the Salam he would not remain seated except long enough to say: (Allahumma antas-salam"""""
"298","Narrated by Ahmad ibn Mani', narrated by Mu'awiyah, from Asim al-Ahwal, from Abdullah ibn al-Harith, from Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her), who said: \When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) concluded the prayer with the salutation (taslim)"
"299","Hannād ibn al-Sarī narrated to us: Marwān ibn Mu'āwiyah al-Fazārī and Abū Mu'āwiyah narrated to us, from ʿĀṣim al-Aḥwal, **through this chain of transmission**, a similar narration, and he said: **\Blessed are You"
"300","Qabisah bin Hulb narrated that his father said:\When Allah's Messenger would lead us in Salat he would turn (to leave) from both sides"""""
"301","Rifa`ah bin Rafi` narrated:\One day Allah's Messenger was sitting in the Masjid\"" Rifa'ah said: \""And we were with him. Then what appeared to be a Bedouin man entered to pray"""""
"302","ʿAlī ibn Ḥuḥr narrated to us — Ismāʿīl ibn Jaʿfar informed us — from Yaḥyā ibn ʿAlī ibn Yaḥyā ibn Khallād ibn Rāfiʿ al-Zuraqī — from his grandfather — from **Rifāʿah ibn Rāfiʿ** (may Allah be pleased with him) that:\n\nThe Messenger of Allah ﷺ was one day sitting in the mosque when Rifāʿah (may Allah be pleased with him) said: \We were with him when a man"
"303","**Muḥammad ibn Bashshār narrated to us:** Yaḥyā ibn Saʿīd al-Qaṭṭān narrated to us: ʿUbayd Allāh ibn ʿUmar narrated to us: Saʿīd ibn Abī Saʿīd informed me, from his father, from Abū Hurayrah (may Allāh be pleased with him) that the Messenger of Allāh (peace and blessings be upon him) entered the mosque, whereupon a man entered and performed ṣalāh. He then came and offered salām upon the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him), and the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) returned his salām and said: **\Go back and perform ṣalāh"
"304","Muhammad ibn Bashshar and Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, saying: Yahya ibn Sa'id al-Qattan narrated to us: Abd al-Hamid ibn Ja'far narrated to us: Muhammad ibn Amr ibn Ata narrated to us from Abu Humayd al-Sa'idi, who said: I heard him while he was among ten of the Companions of the Prophet ﷺ, one of them being Abu Qatadah ibn Rib'i, saying: ""I am the most knowledgeable of you regarding the prayer of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ."" They said: ""You were not the earliest of us in his companionship nor the most frequent in visiting him."" He said: ""Yes, indeed."" They said: ""Then demonstrate."" He said: ""When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ stood for prayer, he stood upright and raised his hands until they were level with his shoulders. When he intended to bow, he raised his hands until they were level with his shoulders, then said: 'Allahu Akbar.' He bowed, then stood straight, neither lowering his head nor raising it high, and placed his hands on his knees. Then he said: 'Sami Allahu liman hamidah.' He raised his hands and stood straight until every bone returned to its place. Then he prostrated, saying: 'Allahu Akbar.' He kept his upper arms away from his sides and spread out the toes of his feet. Then he bent his left foot and sat on it, then stood straight until every bone returned to its place. Then he prostrated, saying: 'Allahu Akbar.' Then he bent his foot and sat, and stood straight until every bone returned to its place. Then he stood up, and did in the second rak'ah the like of that. Until when he stood from the two prostrations, he said the takbir and raised his hands until they were level with his shoulders, as he did when he opened the prayer. Then he did likewise until it was the rak'ah in which his prayer concluded; he withdrew his left foot and sat on his side in the tawarruk position, then gave the salam."" Abu Isa said: This is a hasan sahih hadith. He said: The meaning of his saying ""and he raised his hands when he stood from the two prostrations"" means he stood from the two rak'ahs."
"305","Qutbah bin Malik narrated:\I heard Allah's Messenger reciting for Fajr: And tall date palms in the first Rak'ah"""""
"306","\I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ recite in the Fajr prayer: **'And the tall palm trees'** (Qur'an 50:10) in the first rakʿah.\""\n\nHe (the narrator) said: \""And in this chapter (there are narrations) from ʿAmr ibn Ḥurayth"
"307","Umm Al-Fadl narrated:\Allah's Messenger came out to us with his head bandaged from his illness. He prayed Maghrib"""""
"308","Abdullah bin Buraidah narrated that his father (Buraidah) said:\Allah's Messenger would recite: By the sun and its brightness"""""
"309","Al-Bara bin Azib narrated:\The Prophet would recite: By the fig and the olive for Isha"""""
"310","Ubadah bin As-Samit narrated:\Allah's Messenger prayed the Subh prayer"""""
"311","Abu Hurairah narrated:\Allah's Messenger turned (after praying) from a Salat in which he recited aloud and said: 'Has any one of you recite along with me just now?' A man said: 'Yes"""""
"312","Al-Ansari narrated to us: Ma'n narrated to us: Malik ibn Anas narrated to us from Ibn Shihab, from Ibn Uqaymah al-Laythi, from Abu Hurayrah, that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ turned away from a prayer in which he recited aloud, and said: ""Did any of you recite with me just now?"" A man said: ""Yes, O Messenger of Allah."" He said: ""I say: What is wrong with me that I am contending with the Qur'an?"" The people then ceased reciting along with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ in those prayers in which he recited aloud, when they heard that from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. He said: In this chapter there are narrations from Ibn Mas'ud, Imran ibn Husayn, and Jabir ibn Abd Allah. Abu Isa said: This is a hasan hadith. Ibn Uqaymah al-Laythi's name is Umayrah, and it is also said Amr ibn Uqaymah. Some companions of al-Zuhri narrated this hadith and mentioned this wording: al-Zuhri said: ""The people ceased reciting when they heard that from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ."" There is nothing in this hadith that affects the view of one who sees recitation behind the imam, because Abu Hurayrah is the one who narrated this hadith from the Prophet ﷺ, and Abu Hurayrah also narrated from the Prophet ﷺ that he said: ""Whoever performs a prayer in which he does not recite Umm al-Qur'an, it is deficient, it is deficient, not complete."" The transmitter of the hadith said to him: ""I am sometimes behind the imam."" He said: ""Recite it in yourself."" Abu Uthman al-Nahdi narrated from Abu Hurayrah that the Prophet ﷺ commanded him to announce: ""There is no prayer except with the recitation of the Opening of the Book."" The majority of the people of hadith chose that the man should not recite when the imam recites aloud, and said: He follows the pauses of the imam. The people of knowledge differed regarding recitation behind the imam. The majority of the people of knowledge among the Companions of the Prophet ﷺ, the Tabi'in, and those after them saw recitation behind the imam, and this is the view of Malik ibn Anas, Abd Allah ibn al-Mubarak, al-Shafi'i, Ahmad, and Ishaq. It is narrated from Abd Allah ibn al-Mubarak that he said: ""I recite behind the imam, and the people recite, except a group of Kufans; and I see that the prayer of one who does not recite is valid."" A group of people of knowledge were strict about leaving the recitation of Fatihat al-Kitab even if behind the imam, saying: ""No prayer is valid except with the recitation of Fatihat al-Kitab, whether alone or behind the imam."" They relied on what Ubadah ibn al-Samit narrated from the Prophet ﷺ. Ubadah ibn al-Samit recited behind the imam after the Prophet ﷺ, and interpreted the Prophet's ﷺ saying: ""There is no prayer except with the recitation of Fatihat al-Kitab."" Al-Shafi'i, Ishaq, and others hold this view. As for Ahmad ibn Hanbal, he said: The meaning of the Prophet's ﷺ saying ""There is no prayer for one who does not recite Fatihat al-Kitab"" is when he is alone. He cited as evidence the hadith of Jabir ibn Abd Allah where he said: ""Whoever performs a rak'ah and does not recite Umm al-Qur'an in it has not prayed, except if he is behind the imam."" Ahmad ibn Hanbal said: This is a man from the Companions of the Prophet ﷺ who interpreted the Prophet's ﷺ saying ""There is no prayer for one who does not recite Fatihat al-Kitab"" as being when he is alone. Ahmad chose, along with this, recitation behind the imam, and that the man should not leave Fatihat al-Kitab even if behind the imam."
"313","Fatimah the Great narrated:\When Allah's Messenger entered the Masjid he said Salat and Salam upon Muhammad and then said: (Rabbighfirli dhunubi"""""
"314","Ismail bin Ibrahim (a narrator in the chain of Hadith no. 314) said:\I met Abdullah bin al Husain in Makkah"""""
"315","Abu Qatadah narrated that :Allah's Messenger said: \When one of you comes to the Masjid"""""
"316","Abu Sa'eed Al-Khudri narrated that :Allah's Messenger said: \All of the earth is a Masjid except for the graveyard and the washroom"""""
"317","Uthman bin Affan narrated that :he heard Allah's Messenger say: \Whoever builds a Masjid for (the sake of) Allah"""""
"318","It has been related that :the Prophet said: \Whoever builds a Masjid for (the sake of) Allah"""""
"319","Ibn Abbbas narrated:\Allah's Messenger cursed the women who visit the graves"""""
"320","Ibn Umar narrated:\We would sleep in the Masjid during the time of Allah's Messenger and we were young men"""""
"321","**Narrated by Ibn ʿUmar (may Allāh be pleased with both of them):**\n\nHe said: \We used to sleep in the mosque during the time of the Messenger of Allāh (peace and blessings be upon him) while we were young men.\""""""""\n\n**Abū ʿĪsā (al-Tirmidhī) said:** The Hadith of Ibn ʿUmar is a *ḥasan ṣaḥīḥ* Hadith.\n\nA group of the people of knowledge granted permission for sleeping in the mosque. Ibn ʿAbbās (may Allāh be pleased with both of them) said: \""""""""One should not take it as a place of overnight lodging (*mabīt*) nor as a place of midday rest (*maqīl*).\"""""""" And a group of the people of knowledge inclined toward the statement of Ibn ʿAbbās.\n\n**Source:** *Jāmiʿ al-Tirmidhī*"""""""""""
"322","Abu Sa'eed Al-Khudri narrated:\A man from Banu Khudrah and a man from Banu Amr bin Awf were disputing about the Masjid that was founded upon Taqwa. The man from Banu Khudrah said: 'It is the Masjid of Allah's Messenger.' The other one said that it was Masjid Qub. So they went to ask Allah's Messenger about that. He said: 'It is this - meaning his Masjid - 'and in that one (Masjid Quba) there is much good"""""
"323","Abu Al-Abrad the freed slave of Banu Khatmah narrated that he heard Usaid bin Zuhair Al-Ansari - and he was one of the Companions of the Prophet - narrated that :the Prophet said: \The Salat in Masjid Quba is like Umrah"""""
"324","Abu Hurairah narrated that :Allah's Messenger said: \Salat is this Masjid of mine is better than a thousand Salat in another"""""
"325","Abu Sa'eed Al-Khudri narrated that :Allah's Messenger said: \A mount is not saddled (for a journey) except to three Masajid: Al-Masjid Al-Haram"""""
"326","Abu Hurairah narrated that :Allah's Messenger said: \When the Iqamah is called for Salat do not come to it rushing"""""
"327","(Another chain with a similar narration) from Abu Hurairah :[from the Prophet]. And this is more correct than the Hadith of Yazid bin Zurai. (no)"
"328","Al-Ḥasan ibn ʿAlī al-Khallāl narrated to us, ʿAbd al-Razzāq narrated to us, Maʿmar informed us, from al-Zuhrī, from Saʿīd ibn al-Musayyab, from Abū Hurayrah, from the Prophet, peace and blessings be upon him, a narration similar in meaning to the ḥadīth of Abū Salamah from Abū Hurayrah. Thus did ʿAbd al-Razzāq state it, from Saʿīd ibn al-Musayyab, from Abū Hurayrah, from the Prophet, peace and blessings be upon him. And this is more authentic than the ḥadīth of Yazīd ibn Zurayʿ."
"329","Abu Hurairah narrated that :Allah's Messenger said: \One of you does not cease to be in Salat as long as he is waiting for it. And the angels do not cease praying for one of you as long as he remains in the Masjid (saying): 'Allah! Forgive him. O Allah! Have mercy upon him' - as long as he does not commit Hadath.\"" A man from Hadramawt said: \""And just what is Hadath Abu Hurairah?\"" He said: \""Breaking wind"""""
"330","Abu Hurairah narrated that :Allah's Messenger said: ""One of you does not cease to be in Salat as long as he is waiting for it. And the angels do not cease praying for one of you as long as he remains in the Masjid (saying): 'Allah! Forgive him. O Allah! Have mercy upon him' - as long as he does not commit Hadath."" A man from Hadramawt said: ""And just what is Hadath Abu Hurairah?"" He said: ""Breaking wind, or passing gas"
"331","Qutaybah narrated to us — Abu al-Ahwāṣ narrated to us — from Simāk ibn Harb — from ʿIkrimah — from Ibn ʿAbbās, who said: **\The Messenger of Allah"
"332","Anas bin Malik narrated:\Allah's Messenger used to mingle with us such that he said to my younger brother: 'O Abu Umair! What did the Nughair do?'\"" He (Anas) said: \""A Bisat of ours would be sprinkled (with water) to perform Salat on"""""
"333","Mu'adh ibn Jabal narrated:\The Prophet liked to perform Salat in Al-Hitan"""""
"334","Muba bin Talhah narrated from his father (Talhah) that :Allah's Messenger said: \When one of you placed something like the post (handle) of the camel saddle in front of him"""""
"335","Zaid bin Khalid Al-Juhni sent a message to Abu Juhaim asking him what he had heard from Allah's Messenger about passing in front of a person who was performing Salat. Abu Juhaim said :that Allah's Messenger said: \If the one who passed in front of the person performing Salat knew what he was doing"""""
"336","Ibn Abbas narrated:\I was a companion rider on a female donkey with Al-Fadl. We came while the Prophet and his Companions were performing Salat at Mina.\"" He said: \""We dismounted from it and joined the row. The donkey then passed in front of them"""""
"337","Ibn Abbas narrated:""I was a companion rider on a female donkey with Al-Fadl. We came while the Prophet and his Companions were performing Salat at Mina."" He said: ""We dismounted from it and joined the row. The donkey then passed in front of them, and this did not invalidate their Salat"
"338","Umar bin Abi Salamah narrated that he saw :Allah's Messenger performing Salat in the house of Umm Salamah wrapped in one garment"
"339","Umar bin Abi Salamah narrated that he saw :Allah's Messenger performing Salat in the house of Umm Salamah wrapped in one garment"
"340","Al-Bara bin Azib narrated:""When Allah's Messener arrived in Al-Madinah, he faced Bait Al-Maqdis in Salat for sixteen or seventeen months. Allah's Messenger longed to face the direction of the Ka'bah, so Allah Most High revealed: Verily! We have seen the turning of your face towards the heaven. Surely We shall turn you o a Qiblah that shall please you. So turn your face in the direction of Al-Masjid Al-Haram.So he faced the Ka'bah, and he liked that. A man performed the Asr prayer with him, then passed by some of the Ansar who were bowing in Salat for Asr while facing Bait Al-Maqdis."" He told them that he had faced the direction of the Ka'bah, so they changed (their direction) while they were bowing."" [He said:] There are narrations on this topic from Ibn Umar, Ibn Abbas, Umarah bin Aws, Amr bin Awf Al-Muzani and Anas"
"341","Abu Hurairah narrated that :Allah's Messenger said: \What is between the east and the west is Qiblah"""""
"342","Abu Hurairah narrated:(Another chain with a similar narration)"
"343","(Another chain narrating that) Abu Hurairah narrated that :Allah's Messenger said: \What is between the east and the west is Qiblah"""""
"344","Abdullah bin Amir bin Rabi'ah narrated from his father who said:\We were with the Prophet on a journey on a very dark night and we did not know the direction of the Qiblah. So each man among us prayed in his own direction. In the morning when we mentioned that to the Prophet"""""
"345","Ibn Umar narrated:\The Prophet prohibited Salat from being performed in seven places: the dung heap"""""
"346","**Narrated by Ibn ʿUmar** (may Allāh be pleased with both of them) that the Messenger of Allāh (peace and blessings be upon him) **forbade** (praying) in **seven places**: the **dunghill** (al-Mazbalah), the **slaughterhouse** (al-Majzarah), the **graveyard** (al-Maqbarah), the **middle of the road** (Qāriʿat al-Ṭarīq), the **bathhouse** (al-Ḥammām), the **camel pens** (resting places of camels) (Maʿāṭin al-Ibil), and **upon the roof of the House of Allāh** (the Sacred Mosque).\n\n- **Maḥmūd ibn Ghaylān** → **al-Muqriʾ** → **Yaḥyā ibn Ayyūb** → **Zayd ibn Jabīrah** → **Dāwūd ibn al-Ḥuṣayn** → **Nāfiʿ** → **Ibn ʿUmar** (may Allāh be pleased with both of them).\n\nThis Hadith establishes the prohibition of performing ṣalāh (prayer) in locations deemed impure, disrespectful, or inappropriate for worship. The seven locations cited include places of filth, slaughter, burial, public thoroughfares, bathhouses, areas where camels gather, and the roof of the Sacred Mosque (al-Masjid al-Ḥarām). The ruling reflects the principle of maintaining the sanctity and purity required for prayer, as well as avoiding places associated with impurity (najāsah) or disrespect to sacred spaces."
"347","Abu Hurairah narrated that :Allah's Messenger said: \Perform Salat in sheep pens but do not perform Salat in the camels' resting area"""""
"348","Abu Kurayb narrated to us: Yahya ibn Adam narrated to us, from Abu Bakr ibn Ayyash, from Hisham, from Ibn Sirin, from Abu Hurayrah (may Allah be pleased with him), who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: \Pray in the resting places of sheep"
"349","(Another chain) from Abu Hurairah, :from the Prophet and it is the same or similar"
"350","Jabir narrated:\The Prophet dispatched me for something he needed. I came to him while he was performing Salat on his mount"""""
"351","Jabir narrated:""The Prophet dispatched me for something he needed. I came to him while he was performing Salat on his mount, heading east, he made the prostrations lower than the bowing"
"352","Anas conveyed that :the Prophet said: \When supper is present and the Iqamah for Salat has been called"""""
"353","Ibn Umar narrated that:the Prophet said: \When the supper is presented and the Iqamah is called for Salat"""""
"354","Aishah narrated that :Allah's Messenger said: \When one of you is sleepy and he is performing Salat"""""
"355","Abu Atiyyah narrated that :a man among them said: \Malik bin Al-Huwairith came to us in our Musalla to narrate. One day when it was time for Salat"""""
"356","Thawban narrated that :the Prophet said: \It is not allowed for a man to look into the interior of a man's house until he has been given permission"""""
"357","Anas bin Malik narrated:\Allah's Messenger cursed three people: A man who leads people (in Salat) while they dislike him"""""
"358","Amr bin Al-Harith Al-Mustaliq said:\It used to be said that the people with the worst punishment [on the Day of Judgment] are two: A woman who disobeyed her husband"""""
"359","Abu Umamah narrated that :Allah's Messenger said: \There are three whose Salat would not rise up beyond their ears: The runaway slave until he returns"""""
"360","Anas bin Malik narrated:\Allah's Messenger fell from a horse and got injured"""""
"361","Anas bin Malik narrated:""Allah's Messenger fell from a horse and got injured, so he led Salat sitting and we also offered Salat sitting. When he completed the Salat he said: ""The Imam is appointed to be followed; when he says the Takbir then say the Takbir, when he bows, then bow, and when he raises his head, then raise your heads. When he says: ""Sami' Allahu liman hamidah (Allah listens to those who praise him)"" then say: ""Rabbana wa lakal-hamd. (O our Lord! And all praise is Yours.)"" and when he prostrates, then prostrate, and when he performs Salat sitting, then pray sitting altogether"
"362","Anas narrated:\Allah's Messenger performed Salat during his illness behind Abu Bakr while seated"""""
"363","Anas narrated:\Allah's Messenger performed Salat during his illness behind Abu Bakr while seated"
"364","Ziyad bin Haqah narrated:\Al-Mughirah bin Shu'bah les us in Salat. When he prayed two Rak'ah he stood without sitting. Those who were behind him said 'Subhan Allah' and he indicated to them that they should stand. He said the Taslim when he had finished his Salat and he performed two prostrations of As-Sahw"""""
"365","Ubaidullah bin Abdullah bin Mas'ud narrated from his father (Abdullah bin Mas'ud) that he said:\When Allah's Messenger sat for the first two Rak'ah it was as if he was on hot stones.\"" Shu'bah (one of the narrators) said: \""Then Sa'd's lips moved (saying) something. So I said: 'Until he stood?' He said: 'Until he stood"""""
"366","Suhaib narrated:\I passed by Allah's Messenger (S) while he was performing Salat"""""
"367","Ibn Umar narrated:\I said to Bilal: 'How did the Prophet (S) reply to them when they gave him Salams and he was performing Salat?' He said: 'He would motion with his hand"""""
"368","Abu Hurairah narrated that:Allah's Messenger said: \The Tasbih is for the men and clapping is for the women"""""
"369","Abu Hurairah narrated that the Prophet (ﷺ) said:\Yawning in prayer (salah) is from the Shaitan"""""
"370","Imran bin Husain narrated:\I asked Allah's Messenger (S) about the Salat for a man who is sitting. He said: 'Whoever performs Salat while standing then that is more virtuous. And whoever performs Salat while sitting"""""
"371","This Hadith has been related from Ibrahim bin Tahman with this chain. Except that he said:\From Imran bin Husain who said: 'I asked Allah's Messenger (S) about Salat for a sick person. He said: \""He performs Salat standing"""""
"372","This Hadith has been narrated through this chain of narration from Ibrāhīm ibn Ṭahmān, except that he narrates it from ʿImrān ibn Ḥuṣayn, who said: \I asked the Messenger of Allah"
"373","Aishah narrated:\The Prophet (S) would perform Salat while sitting. And he would recite while sitting. When about thirty or forty Ayah of his recitation remained he would standup and recite while he was standing"""""
"374","Narrated by al-Ansari, narrated by Ma'n, narrated by Malik, from Abu al-Nadr, from Abu Salamah, from Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her), that the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) used to pray while sitting, reciting while seated. When approximately thirty or forty verses of his recitation remained, he would stand and recite while standing, then bow and prostrate. He would do the same in the second rak'ah.\n\nAbu Isa (al-Tirmidhi) said: This is a hasan sahih hadith."
"375","Anas bin Malik narrated that:Allah's Messenger said: \Indeed I hear the crying of a small boy while I am in Salat"""""
"376","Aishah narrated that:Allah's Messenger said: \The Salat of a women who has reached the age of menstruation is not accepted without a Khimar"""""
"377","Aishah narrated that:Allah's Messenger said: ""The Salat of a women who has reached the age of menstruation is not accepted without a Khimar"
"378","Abu Dharr narrated that :the Prophet (S) said: \When one of you stands for Salat then he should not smoothen the pebbles"""""
"379","Mu'aiqib narrated:\I asked Allah's Messenger (S) about smoothening the pebbles during Salat. He said: 'If you must do so"""""
"380","Umm Salamah narrated:\The Prophet (S) saw a boy of ours - called Aflah - blowing when he prostrated. So he said: 'O Aflah! Put your face in the dirt"""""
"381","(Another chain) in which Abu Hamzah narrated:\A boy of ours named Rabah"""""
"382","Abu Hurairah narrated:\The Prophet (S) prohibited than a man to pray with his hands on his hip"""""
"383","Abu Rafi narrated that :He passed by Al-Hasan bin Ali while he was performing Salat and he had gathered his locks at the back of his head"
"384","Al-Fadl bin Al-`Abbas narrated that:Allah's Messenger (S) said: \As-Salat is two and two"""""
"385","Ka'b bun Ujrah narrated that:Allah's Messenger (S) said: \When one of you performs Wudu and does so well"""""
"386","Jabir narrated:\It was said to the Prophet (S): 'Which Salat is most virtuous?' He said: 'That with the longest Qunut"""""
"387","Ma'dan bin Talhah Al Yamari said:\I met Thawban the freed slave of Allah's Messenger (S) and said to him"""""
"388","Narrated to us was Abu 'Ammār, to whom narrated al-Walīd, who said — and narrated to us Abū Muḥammad Rajā', who said — narrated to us al-Walīd ibn Muslim, from al-Awzā'ī, who said — narrated to me al-Walīd ibn Hishām al-Mu'ayṭī, who said — narrated to me Ma'dān ibn Ṭalḥah al-Ya'marī, who said:\n\nI met Thawbān, the freed slave of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and I said to him: \Direct me to a deed by which Allah will benefit me and through which He will admit me to Paradise.\"" He remained silent for a long while"
"389","Abu Hurairah narrated:\Allah's Messenger (S) ordered killing the two black things in Salat; the snake and the scorpion"""""
"390","Abu Hurairah narrated:""Allah's Messenger (S) ordered killing the two black things in Salat; the snake and the scorpion"
"391","Ibn Abbas narrated that :the Prophet said: \Jibril (peace be upon him) led me (in Salat) twice at the House. So he prayed Zuhr the first time when the shadow was similar to (the length of) the strap a sandal. Then he prayed Asr when everything was similar (to the length of) its shadow. Then he prayed Maghrib when the sun had set and the fasting person breaks fast. Then he prayed Isha when the twilight had vanished. Then he prayed Fajr when Fajr (dawn) began"""""
"392","Muhammad ibn Bashshar narrated to us: Abd al-A'la and Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Hisham narrated to us from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, from Muhammad ibn Ibrahim, that Abu Hurayrah and al-Sa'ib al-Qari used to perform the two prostrations of forgetfulness before the salam. Abu Isa said: The hadith of Ibn Buhaynah is hasan sahih. The practice is upon this according to some people of knowledge, and it is the view of al-Shafi'i: he sees all prostrations of forgetfulness before the salam, and says this abrogates other hadiths, and mentions that the last action of the Prophet ﷺ was upon this. Ahmad and Ishaq said: If the man stands up in the two rak'ahs, then he performs the two prostrations of forgetfulness before the salam, based on the hadith of Ibn Buhaynah. Abd Allah ibn Buhaynah is Abd Allah ibn Malik; Malik is his father and Buhaynah is his mother. Thus Ishaq ibn Mansur informed me from Ali ibn Abd Allah ibn al-Madini. Abu Isa said: The people of knowledge differed regarding the two prostrations of forgetfulness: when does the man perform them, before the salam or after it? Some saw that he should perform them after the salam. This is the view of Sufyan al-Thawri and the people of Kufa. Some said he should perform them before the salam. This is the view of the majority of the jurists of the people of Madinah, such as Yahya ibn Sa'id, Rabi'ah, and others, and al-Shafi'i holds this view. Some said: If it is an addition in the prayer, then after the salam; if it is a deficiency, then before the salam. This is the view of Malik ibn Anas. Ahmad said: Whatever is narrated from the Prophet ﷺ regarding the two prostrations of forgetfulness is to be acted upon, each according to its context. He sees that if he stood up in the two rak'ahs, based on the hadith of Ibn Buhaynah, then he performs them before the salam; if he prayed Zuhr as five rak'ahs, then he performs them after the salam; if he gave salam in two rak'ahs of Zuhr and Asr, then he performs them after the salam; each is acted upon according to its context. And every forgetfulness in which there is no mention from the Prophet ﷺ, its prostrations are before the salam. Ishaq said something similar to Ahmad in all of this, except that he said: Every forgetfulness in which there is no mention from the Prophet ﷺ, if it is an addition in the prayer, he performs them after the salam; if it is a deficiency, he performs them before the salam."
"393","Abdullah (bin Masud) narrated:\The Prophet (S) performed two prostrations for As-Sahw after talking"""""
"394","Abu Hurairah narrated:\The Prophet (S) performed two prostrations after the Salam"""""
"395","Abu Al-Muhallab narrated from Imran bin Husain that :the Prophet (S) led them in Salat he forgot (something) so he performed two prostrations"
"396","Iyad bin Hilal said:\I said to Abu Sa'eed: 'One of us performs Salat and we do not know how (much) we prayed.' So he said: 'Allah's Messenger (S) said: \""When one of you performs Salat and he does now know how (much) he prayed then let him perform two prostrations while he is sitting"""""
"397","Abu Hurairah narrated that:Allah's Messenger (S) said: \Indeed the Shaitan comes to one of you in his Salat confusing him until he does now know how much he has prayed. When one of you experiences that then let him perform two prostrations while sitting"""""
"398","Abdur-Rahman bi Awf narrated that he heard the Prophet (S) saying:\When one of you becomes forgetful in his Salat so that he does not know if he prayed one or two"""""
"399","Abu Hurairah narrated:\The Prophet (S) turned (finished the prayer) after two (Rak'ah)"""""
"400","Sa'eed bin Yazid Abu Maslamah said:\I said to Anas bin Malik: 'Would Allah's Messenger (S) perform Salat wearing his sandals?' He said: 'Yes"""""
"401","Al-Bara bin Azib narrated:\The Prophet (S) would perform the Qunut in the Subh and Maghrib prayers"""""
"402","Abu Malik Al-Ashjai narrated:\I said to my father: 'O my father! You offered Salat behind Allah's Messenger (S)"""""
"403","There is another narration from Abu Malik:There exists another narration from Abu Malik with similar meaning but with different chain"
"404","Muadh bin Rifa'ah narrated that his father said:\I prayed behind Allah's Messenger (S). I sneezed and said: Al-Hamdulillah"""""
"405","Zaid bin Arqam narrated:\We used to talk behind Allah's Messenger (S) during the Salat"""""
"406","Asma bin Al-Hakam Al-Fazari said:""I heard Ali saying: 'Indeed I am a man who, when I heard a Hadith from Allah's Messenger (S) then Allah causes me to benefit from it as much as He wills for me to benefit from it. When a man among his Companions narrated to me I ask him to swear an oath to me about it, and when he swears an oath to me I trust him. And Abu Bakr narrated to me - and Abu Bakr told the truth - he said: ""I heard Allah's Messenger (S) saying: 'There is no man who commits a sin, then makes Wudu, then performs Salat, then seeks forgiveness from Allah, except that Allah forgives him.' Then he recited this Ayah: Those who when they have committed Fahishah or wronged themselves with eveil, remember Allah. (3:135) until the end of the Ayah"
"407","(Sabrah bin Ma'bad al-Juhni) narrated that:Allah's Messenger (S) said: \Teach the boy Salat when he is seven years old"""""
"408","Abdullah bin Amr narrated that:Allah's Messenger (S) said: \When he commits Hadath - meaning a man - and he is sitting in the end of his Salat before saying the Taslim"""""
"409","Jabir narrated:\We were with the Prophet (S) on a journey when it started to rain on us"""""
"410","Ibn Abbas narrated:\Some of the poor people came to Allah's Messenger (S) and said: 'O Messenger of Allah (S)! The rich pray as we pray"""""
"411","Ishaq ibn Ibrahim ibn Habib ibn al-Shahid al-Basri and Ali ibn Hujr narrated to us, saying: Attab ibn Bashir narrated to us from Khusayf, from Mujahid and Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, who said: The poor came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and said: ""O Messenger of Allah, the rich pray as we pray and fast as we fast, and they have wealth with which they free slaves and give charity."" He said: ""When you pray, say Subhan Allah thirty-three times, Alhamdulillah thirty-three times, Allahu Akbar thirty-four times, and La ilaha illa Allah ten times. You will thereby overtake those who preceded you, and none after you will overtake you."" He said: In this chapter there are narrations from Ka'b ibn Ujrah, Anas, Abd Allah ibn Amr, Zayd ibn Thabit, Abu al-Darda, Ibn Umar, and Abu Dharr. Abu Isa said: The hadith of Ibn Abbas is hasan gharib. In this chapter there is also from Abu Hurayrah and al-Mughirah. It has been narrated from the Prophet ﷺ that he said: ""Two characteristics, no Muslim man enumerates them except he enters Paradise: he glorifies Allah after every prayer ten times, praises Him ten times, magnifies Him ten times; and when he goes to bed he glorifies Allah thirty-three times, praises Him thirty-three times, and magnifies Him thirty-four times."""""
"412","Al-Mughirah bin Shu'bah narrated:\Allah's Messenger (S) performed Salat until his feet were swollen"""""
"413","Huraith bin Qabisah narrated:\I arrived in Al-Madinah and said: 'O Allah! Facilitate me to be in a righteous gathering.'\"" He said: \""I sat with Abu Hurairah and said: 'Indeed I asked Allah to provide me with a righteous gathering. So narrate a hadith to me which you heard from Allah's Messenger (ﷺ) so that perhaps Allah would cause me to benefit from it.' He said: 'I heard Allah's Messenger (ﷺ) say: \""Indeed the first deed by which a servant will be called to account on the Day of Resurrection is his Salat. If it is complete"""""
"414","Aishah narrated that Allah's Messenger (S) said:\Whoever is regular with twelve Rak'ah of Sunnah (prayer)"""""
"415","Umm Habibah narrated that Allah's Messenger (S) sad:\Whoever prays twelve Rak'ah in a day and night"""""
"416","Aishah narrated that :Allah's Messenger (S) said: \The two Rak'ah of Fajr are better than the world and what is in it"""""
"417","Ibn Umar narrated:\I watched the Prophet (S) for a month. In the two Rak'ah before Fajr he would recite: Say: \""O you disbelievers!\"" and Say: \""Allah is One"""""
"418","Aishah narrated:\When Allah's Messenger (S) prayed the two Rak'ah (before) Fajr if he needed something from me he would talk to me"""""
"419","Ibn Umar narrated that:Allah's Messenger (S) said: \There is no Salat after Al-Fajr (begins) except two prostrations"""""
"420","Abu Hurairah narrated that:Allah's Messenger (S) said: \When one of you prays the two Rak'ah of Fajr then let him lay down on his right (side)"""""
"421","Abu Hurairah narrated that:Allah's Messenger (S) said: \When the Iqamah has been called for the Salat then there is no Salat except the obligatory"""""
"422","Qais narrated:\Allah's Messenger (S) went out and the Iqamah was called for the Salat so I prayed As-Subh with him. Then the Prophet (S) turned and found me performing Salat so he said: 'Easy O Qais! Are there two prayers together?' I said: 'O Messenger of Allah! I did not perform the two Rak'ah (before) Fajr.' He said: 'Then there is no harm"""""
"423","Abu Hurairah narrated that:Allah's Messenger (S) said: \Whoever did not pray the two Rak'ah (before) Fajr then let him pray them after the sun has risen"""""
"424","Ali narrated:\The Prophet (S) would pray four Rak'ah before Az-Zuhr and two Rak'ah after it"""""
"425","Ibn Umar narrated:\I prayed two Rak'ah with the Prophet (S) before Az-Zuhr and two Rak'ah after it"""""
"426","Aishah narrated:\When the Prophet (S) would not perform the four Rak'ah before Az-Zuhr he would pray them after it"""""
"427","Umm Habibah narrated that:Allah's Messenger (S) said: \Whoever prays four before Az-Zuhr and four after"""""
"428","Umm Habibah the wife of the Prophet (S) narrated that:She heard Allah's Messenger (S) saying: \Whoever maintains four Rak'ah before Az-Zuhr and four after it"""""
"429","Ali narrated:\Allah's Messenger (S) would pray four Rak'ah before Al-Asr separating between them with At-Taslim upon the angels that are close (to Allah) and those who follow them among the Muslims and the believers"""""
"430","Ibn Umar narrated that :The Prophet (S) said: \May Allah have mercy upon a man who prays four before Al-Asr"""""
"431","Abdullah bin Mas'ud narrated:\I can not enumerate (how many times) I heard Allah's Messenger (S) reciting - in the two Rak'ah after Al-Maghrib and the two Rak'ah before Salatul-Fajr with: Say: \""O you disbelievers!\"" and Say: \""He is Allah the One"""""
"432","Ibn Umar narrated:\I prayed two Rak'ah after Al-Maghrib with the Prophet (S) in his house"""""
"433","Ibn Umar narrated:\I memorized ten Rak'ah from Allah's Messenger (S) which he would pray in a night and a day: Two Rak'ah before Az-Zuhr"""""
"434","Narrated by al-Ḥasan ibn ʿAlī al-Ḥulwānī al-Khallāl, who narrated from ʿAbd al-Razzāq, who reported from Maʿmar, from Ayyūb, from Nāfiʿ, from Ibn ʿUmar (may Allāh be pleased with them both), who said:\n\n\I preserved from the Messenger of Allāh (peace and blessings be upon him) ten rakʿahs that he used to perform during the night and the day: two rakʿahs before the Ẓuhr prayer"
"435","Abu Hurairah narrated that:Allah's Messenger (S) said: \Whoever prays six Rak'ah after Al-Maghrib"""""
"436","Abdullah bin Shaqiq said:\I asked Aishah about the Salat of Allah's Messenger (S). She said: 'He would pray four Rak'ah before Az-Zuhr and two Rak'ah after it"""""
"437","Ibn Umar narrated that:The Prophet (S) said: \Salat in the night is two by two. So when you fear the dawn (is near) then make it odd by one"""""
"438","Abu Hurairah narrated that:Allah's Messenger (S) said: \The most virtuous fasting after the month of Ramadan is that of Allah's month of Al-Muharram. And the most virtuous Salat after the obligatory is the night prayer"""""
"439","Sa'eed bin Abi Sa'eed Al-Maqburi narrated that:Sa'eed bin Abi Sa'eed Al-Maqburi narrated that Abu Salamah informed him that he had asked Aishah: \How was the Salat of Allah's Messenger (A) [at night] during Ramadan?\"" She said: \""Allah's Messenger (S) would pray - neither in Ramadan nor in any other month - more than eleven Rak'ah. He would pray four"""""
"440","Aishah narrated:""Allah's Messenger (S) would pray eleven Rak'ah at night, making them off with one. When he finished them he would lay down on his right side"
"441","Narrated to us al-Ḥasan ibn ‘Alī al-‘Askarī, narrated to us Abū Bakr ibn Abī al-Isḥāq, narrated to us Muḥammad ibn Kathīr, narrated to us Sufyān, from Abū Isḥāq, from ‘Āmir al-Sha‘bī, from Masrūq, from ‘Ā’isha (may Allāh be pleased with her), that she said: \Between the ‘Ishā’ prayer and the Fajr prayer"
"442","Ibn Abbas narrated:\The Prophet (S) would pray thirteen Rak'ah at night"""""
"443","Aishah narrated:\The Prophet (S) would pray nine Rak'ah in the night"""""
"444","Narrator not mentioned:(Another chain with similar narration)"
"445","Aishah narrated:\When the Prophet (S) did not pray at night because he was prevented from it by sleep or being sleepy then he would pray twelve Rak'ah during the daytime"""""
"446","Abu Hurairah narrated that:Allah's Messenger (S) said: ""Allah, Blessed and Exalted is He, descends to the earth's heaven every night when the first third of the night has passed. He says: ""I am the Sovereign. Is there any who calls upon Me so that I may respond to him? Is there any who asks of Me that I may give him? Is there any who seeks forgiveness from Me so that I may forgive him?' He continues in that until the illumination of Al-Fajr"
"447","Abu Qatadah narrated that :The Prophet (S) said to Abu Bakr: \I passed by you while you were reciting and your voice was low.\"" He said: \""I let He who"""""
"448","Aishah narrated:\The Prophet (S) stood (in prayer) with an Ayah from the Qur'an at night"""""
"449","Abdullah bin Abi Qais narrated:\I asked Aishah how the recitation of the Prophet (S) was at night. [Would he recite silently o audibly?] So she said: 'He would do both of those. Sometimes he was silent with his recitation and sometimes it was audible.' So I said: 'All praise is due to Allah"""""
"450","Zaid bin Thabit narrated that:The Prophet (S) said: \The most virtuous prayer of yours is in your homes"""""
"451","Ibn Umar narrated that :The Prophet (S) said: \Offer Salat in your homes and do not turn them into graves"""""
